For example, classical realism is a contemporary style combining elements of 19th century neoclassicism and realism.    While Neoclassicism ""emerged as a Western cultural movement in the decorative and visual arts, literature, theatre, music, and architecture that drew inspiration from the art and culture of classical antiquity.""  Ie, there's a direct lineage here.  An active Neoclassical today is Richard T. Scott.  ",565,,,,,,,debounce,,
