5,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,41,Male,sg_1776172728651_xarmvr,diffuse,1,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-14T13:32:47.265Z,,,,,,,"The parts of the brain that help in scientific discoveries and creativity are still not fully understood. However, studies have found that the left hemisphere of the brain is important in scientific discoveries. IMRI investigation found that unexpected findings activated the prefrontal cortex of the brain. Further to this, the default and executive control networks in the brain cooperate during creative tasks, suggesting a complex interaction between these networks in facilitating everyday imaginative thought",514,,,,,,,debounce,,
