8,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,29,Male,sg_1776172775255_phz2jb,clumpy,0,1,practice,practice-capybaras,What do Capybaras eat?,answer_snapshot_cursor_leave,2026-04-14T13:24:17.621Z,,,,,,,"The capybara is a herbivore, meaning it is an animal that evolve to consume plant material. They graze mostly on grasses and aquatic plants, tree bark as well as fruit. Their jaw is not perpendicular, so they chew food by grinding their teeth side to side, as opposed to side to side. They are autocophagous, meaning the eat their own feces.",341,,,,,,,cursor_leave,,
