13,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,38,Male,sg_1776175539831_hxn9r8,diffuse,2,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,paste,2026-04-14T14:22:16.343Z,,,,,,,,,,,"In mammalian brain anatomy, the prefrontal cortex (PFC) covers the front part of the frontal lobe of the human brain. It is the association cortex in the frontal lobe.[2][3] This region is responsible for processing and adapting one's thinking in order to meet certain goals in different situations.[4] These processes of thinking can include the brain allowing one to focus, control how they behave, and make different decisions.[5]",433,,,,,
