13,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,38,Male,sg_1776175539831_hxn9r8,diffuse,2,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-14T14:25:29.151Z,,,,,,,"In mammalian brain anatomy, the prefrontal cortex (PFC) covers the front part of the frontal lobe of the human brain. It is the association cortex in the frontal lobe.This region is responsible for processing and adapting one's thinking in order to meet certain goals in different situations. These processes of thinking can include the brain allowing one to focus, control how they behave, and make different decisions. Put basically, the prefrotnal cortex is resonsible for all the of the tool necessary to enable scientic discovery. It controls cognition, and the ability to filter infomration and tune out irrelevant stimuli. Most importantly it controls memory and the ability to think about multiple concepts at the same time. Two concepts that are essential to make scientic disocveries.",794,,,,,,,debounce,,
