Renaissance art took as its foundation the art of Classical antiquity, perceived as the noblest of ancient traditions, but transformed that tradition by absorbing recent developments in the art of Northern Europe and by applying contemporary scientific knowledge. Along with Renaissance humanist philosophy, it spread throughout Europe, affecting both artists and their patrons with the development of new techniques and new artistic sensibilities. For art historians, Renaissance art marks the transition of Europe from the medieval period to the Early Modern age.

It plays a role in contemporary society as it laid the foundation for the aet ",901,,,,,,,debounce,,
14,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,30,Male,sg_1776177548786_ryltzr,clumpy,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-14T14:50:40.406Z,,,,,,,"their are various types of ancient art but arguably the most impactful on the role of contemporary art is Renaissance art from 1350-1620 as in involves and mastered the techniques that are still used today such as painting sculpting and decorative arts. 

Renaissance art took as its foundation the art of Classical antiquity, perceived as the noblest of ancient traditions, but transformed that tradition by absorbing recent developments in the art of Northern Europe and by applying contemporary scientific knowledge. Along with Renaissance humanist philosophy, it spread throughout Europe, affecting both artists and their patrons with the development of new techniques and new artistic sensibilities. For art historians, Renaissance art marks the transition of Europe from the medieval period to the Early Modern age.

It plays a role in contemporary society as it laid the foundation for the art that is used today and is the bridge between old art and modern art.",969,,,,,,,debounce,,
14,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,30,Male,sg_1776177548786_ryltzr,clumpy,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot_cursor_leave,2026-04-14T14:50:44.228Z,,,,,,,"their are various types of ancient art but arguably the most impactful on the role of contemporary art is Renaissance art from 1350-1620 as in involves and mastered the techniques that are still used today such as painting sculpting and decorative arts. 

Renaissance art took as its foundation the art of Classical antiquity, perceived as the noblest of ancient traditions, but transformed that tradition by absorbing recent developments in the art of Northern Europe and by applying contemporary scientific knowledge. Along with Renaissance humanist philosophy, it spread throughout Europe, affecting both artists and their patrons with the development of new techniques and new artistic sensibilities. For art historians, Renaissance art marks the transition of Europe from the medieval period to the Early Modern age.

It plays a role in contemporary society as it laid the foundation for the art that is used today and is the bridge between old art and modern art.",969,,,,,,,cursor_leave,,
