15,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,34,Female,sg_1776177591849_ac6hd9,clumpy,0,1,practice,practice-capybaras,What do Capybaras eat?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-14T14:54:30.121Z,,,,,,,"The capybara is a herbivore, and mainly feeds on grasses and aquatic plants, but also on fruit and tree bark. The capybara's name means 'one who eats slender leaves', or 'grass eater'. They often feed on the leaves of one particular species and disregard other species surrounding it, making them fussy eaters. However, during the dry season, capybaras eat a greater variety of plants, as fewer plants are present. While they eat grass during the wet season, they have to switch to more abundant reeds during the dry season.[26] The swap to reeds during this season, as more are available, whereas they tend to eat grass during the wet season. The plants that capybaras would usually consume in summer lose their nutritional value by winter, and so capybaras no longer eat these in this season.[27] Capybaras are autocoprophagous,[28] meaning they eat their own feces as a source of bacterial gut flora, to help digest the cellulose in the grass that forms their normal diet, and to extract the maximum protein and vitamins from their food. Capybaras regurgitate food to chew again, and also eat their own feces to help digest the grass and to help extract the most protein and vitamins from their food possible.",1212,,,,,,,debounce,,
15,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,34,Female,sg_1776177591849_ac6hd9,clumpy,0,1,practice,practice-capybaras,What do Capybaras eat?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-14T14:54:48.633Z,,,,,,,"The capybara is a herbivore, and mainly feeds on grasses and aquatic plants, but also on fruit and tree bark. The capybara's name means 'one who eats slender leaves', or 'grass eater'. They often feed on the leaves of one particular species and disregard other species surrounding it, making them fussy eaters. However, during the dry season, capybaras eat a greater variety of plants, as fewer plants are present. While they eat grass during the wet season, they have to switch to more abundant reeds during the dry season.[26] The swap to reeds during this season, as more are available, whereas they tend to eat grass during the wet season. The plants that capybaras would usually consume in summer lose their nutritional value by winter, and so capybaras no longer eat these in this season. Capybaras regurgitate food to chew again, and also eat their own feces to help digest the grass and to help extract the most protein and vitamins from their food possible.",966,,,,,,,debounce,,
