15,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,34,Female,sg_1776177591849_ac6hd9,clumpy,1,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,answer_snapshot_cursor_leave,2026-04-14T15:03:28.872Z,,,,,,,"The frontal lobe in the brain is responsible for actions such as planning, reasoning and abstract thought. These executive functions also include the ability to reason and problem solve, due to its propensity to plan, prospect and use intelligence. Therefore I would assume that the frontal and prefrontal cortex help people to make scientific discoveries, as all of these areas of the brain and decision making would be activated.",431,,,,,,,cursor_leave,,
