25,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,33,Male,sg_1776179264283_o34au0,clumpy,0,1,practice,practice-capybaras,What do Capybaras eat?,paste,2026-04-14T15:16:46.829Z,,,,,,,,,,,"Capybaras are autocoprophagous,[28] meaning they eat their own feces as a source of bacterial gut flora, to help digest the cellulose in the grass that forms their normal diet, and to extract the maximum protein and vitamins from their food.",241,,,,,
25,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,33,Male,sg_1776179264283_o34au0,clumpy,0,1,practice,practice-capybaras,What do Capybaras eat?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-14T15:16:48.836Z,,,,,,,"Capybaras are semiaquatic herbivores and from the meaning of it's common name Tupi ka'apiûara, ""one who eats slender leaves"", we see that they eat grass.

We can also see that they flourish in cattle ranches becasue of the abundance of leaves available.

From the picture of the capybaras grazing we can conclude that capybaras are herbivores, grazing mainly on grasses and aquatic plants as well as fruit and tree bark.

Capybaras are autocoprophagous,[28] meaning they eat their own feces as a source of bacterial gut flora, to help digest the cellulose in the grass that forms their normal diet, and to extract the maximum protein and vitamins from their food.",663,,,,,,,debounce,,
25,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,33,Male,sg_1776179264283_o34au0,clumpy,0,1,practice,practice-capybaras,What do Capybaras eat?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-14T15:16:54.221Z,,,,,,,"Capybaras are semiaquatic herbivores and from the meaning of it's common name Tupi ka'apiûara, ""one who eats slender leaves"", we see that they eat grass.

