From the picture of the capybaras grazing we can conclude that capybaras are herbivores, grazing mainly on grasses and aquatic plants as well as fruit and tree bark.

They eat their own feces as a source of bacterial gut flora, to help digest the cellulose in the grass that forms their normal diet, and to extract the maximum protein and vitamins from their food.",619,,,,,,,debounce,,
