26,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,33,Female,sg_1776179918038_z13a8u,clumpy,1,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-14T15:35:48.456Z,,,,,,,Well-developed prefrontal cortex and parietal lobes have been associated with scientists who have made great discoveries. These areas were also found to be densely packed with neurons. This was found to be the case in both the brains of  Also the absence of a typical groove in the brain known as the 'sylvian fissure' is thought to potentially allow for better communication between different brain regions.,408,,,,,,,debounce,,
26,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,33,Female,sg_1776179918038_z13a8u,clumpy,1,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-14T15:35:55.550Z,,,,,,,Well-developed prefrontal cortex and parietal lobes have been associated with scientists who have made great discoveries. These areas were also found to be densely packed with neurons. This was found to be the case in both the brains of Albert Einstein and Vl Also the absence of a typical groove in the brain known as the 'sylvian fissure' is thought to potentially allow for better communication between different brain regions.,430,,,,,,,debounce,,
26,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,33,Female,sg_1776179918038_z13a8u,clumpy,1,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-14T15:36:04.754Z,,,,,,,Well-developed prefrontal cortex and parietal lobes have been associated with scientists who have made great discoveries. These areas were also found to be densely packed with neurons. This was found to be the case in both the brains of Albert Einstein and Vladimir Lenin. Also the absence of a typical groove in the brain known as the 'sylvian fissure' is thought to potentially allow for better communication between different brain regions.,443,,,,,,,debounce,,
26,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,33,Female,sg_1776179918038_z13a8u,clumpy,1,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-14T15:36:14.127Z,,,,,,,Well-developed prefrontal cortex and parietal lobes have been associated with scientists who have made great discoveries. These areas were also found to be densely packed with neurons. Abundance of neurons was found to be the case in both the brains of Albert Einstein and Vladimir Lenin. Also the absence of a typical groove in the brain known as the 'sylvian fissure' is thought to potentially allow for better communication between different brain regions.,459,,,,,,,debounce,,
26,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,33,Female,sg_1776179918038_z13a8u,clumpy,1,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,answer_snapshot_cursor_leave,2026-04-14T15:36:44.993Z,,,,,,,Well-developed prefrontal cortex and parietal lobes have been associated with scientists who have made great discoveries. These areas were also found to be densely packed with neurons. Abundance of neurons was found to be the case in both the brains of Albert Einstein and Vladimir Lenin. Also the absence of a typical groove in the brain known as the 'sylvian fissure' is thought to potentially allow for better communication between different brain regions.,459,,,,,,,cursor_leave,,
