26,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,33,Female,sg_1776179918038_z13a8u,clumpy,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-14T15:42:36.706Z,,,,,,,From Ancient Egyptian art derived 'Egyptian Revival art',56,,,,,,,debounce,,
26,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,33,Female,sg_1776179918038_z13a8u,clumpy,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot_cursor_leave,2026-04-14T15:42:48.297Z,,,,,,,"From Ancient Egyptian art derived 'Egyptian Revival art' which is a stlye in Western art, mainlg ",97,,,,,,,cursor_leave,,
26,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,33,Female,sg_1776179918038_z13a8u,clumpy,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,paste,2026-04-14T15:43:02.697Z,,,,,,,,,,,"early nineteenth century, in which Egyptian motifs were applied to a wide variety of decorative arts objects. It was underground in American decorative arts throughout the nineteenth century, continuing into the 1920s. The major motifs of Egyptian art, such as obelisks, hieroglyphs, the sphinx, and pyramids, were used in various artistic media, including architecture, furniture, ceramics, and silver. ",404,,,,,
26,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,33,Female,sg_1776179918038_z13a8u,clumpy,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-14T15:43:04.710Z,,,,,,,"From Ancient Egyptian art derived 'Egyptian Revival art' which is a stlye in Western art, main early nineteenth century, in which Egyptian motifs were applied to a wide variety of decorative arts objects. It was underground in American decorative arts throughout the nineteenth century, continuing into the 1920s. The major motifs of Egyptian art, such as obelisks, hieroglyphs, the sphinx, and pyramids, were used in various artistic media, including architecture, furniture, ceramics, and silver. ",499,,,,,,,debounce,,
26,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,33,Female,sg_1776179918038_z13a8u,clumpy,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-14T15:43:07.715Z,,,,,,,"From Ancient Egyptian art derived 'Egyptian Revival art' which is a stlye in Western art, mainly of the early nineteenth century, in which Egyptian motifs were applied to a wide variety of decorative arts objects. It was underground in American decorative arts throughout the nineteenth century, continuing into the 1920s. The major motifs of Egyptian art, such as obelisks, hieroglyphs, the sphinx, and pyramids, were used in various artistic media, including architecture, furniture, ceramics, and silver. ",508,,,,,,,debounce,,
26,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,33,Female,sg_1776179918038_z13a8u,clumpy,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot_cursor_leave,2026-04-14T15:43:16.065Z,,,,,,,"From Ancient Egyptian art derived 'Egyptian Revival art' which is a stlye in Western art, mainly of the early nineteenth century, in which Egyptian motifs were applied to a wide variety of decorative arts objects. It was underground in American decorative arts throughout the nineteenth century, continuing into the 1920s. The major motifs of Egyptian art, such as obelisks, hieroglyphs, the sphinx, and pyramids, were used in various artistic media, including architecture, furniture, ceramics, and silver. ",508,,,,,,,cursor_leave,,
26,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,33,Female,sg_1776179918038_z13a8u,clumpy,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,paste,2026-04-14T15:43:25.792Z,,,,,,,,,,,"Egyptian motifs provided an exotic alternative to the more traditional styles of the day. Over the course of the nineteenth century, American tastes evolved from a highly ornamented aesthetic to a simpler, sparer sense of decoration; the vocabulary of ancient Egyptian art would be interpreted and adapted in different ways depending on the standards and motivations of the time.[138] This legacy endures in contemporary Egyptian art, as seen in the work of Rasha Amin, whose Cairo upbringing shapes her multidisciplinary pieces, reflecting the influence of Egypt’s rich cultural heritage.[139]",594,,,,,
26,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,33,Female,sg_1776179918038_z13a8u,clumpy,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-14T15:43:27.805Z,,,,,,,"From Ancient Egyptian art derived 'Egyptian Revival art' which is a stlye in Western art, mainly of the early nineteenth century, in which Egyptian motifs were applied to a wide variety of decorative arts objects. It was underground in American decorative arts throughout the nineteenth century, continuing into the 1920s. The major motifs of Egyptian art, such as obelisks, hieroglyphs, the sphinx, and pyramids, were used in various artistic media, including architecture, furniture, ceramics, and silver. Egyptian motifs provided an exotic alternative to the more traditional styles of the day. Over the course of the nineteenth century, American tastes evolved from a highly ornamented aesthetic to a simpler, sparer sense of decoration; the vocabulary of ancient Egyptian art would be interpreted and adapted in different ways depending on the standards and motivations of the time.[138] This legacy endures in contemporary Egyptian art, as seen in the work of Rasha Amin, whose Cairo upbringing shapes her multidisciplinary pieces, reflecting the influence of Egypt’s rich cultural heritage.[139]",1102,,,,,,,debounce,,
26,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,33,Female,sg_1776179918038_z13a8u,clumpy,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot_cursor_leave,2026-04-14T15:43:32.549Z,,,,,,,"From Ancient Egyptian art derived 'Egyptian Revival art' which is a stlye in Western art, mainly of the early nineteenth century, in which Egyptian motifs were applied to a wide variety of decorative arts objects. It was underground in American decorative arts throughout the nineteenth century, continuing into the 1920s. The major motifs of Egyptian art, such as obelisks, hieroglyphs, the sphinx, and pyramids, were used in various artistic media, including architecture, furniture, ceramics, and silver. Egyptian motifs provided an exotic alternative to the more traditional styles of the day. Over the course of the nineteenth century, American tastes evolved from a highly ornamented aesthetic to a simpler, sparer sense of decoration; the vocabulary of ancient Egyptian art would be interpreted and adapted in different ways depending on the standards and motivations of the time.[138] This legacy endures in contemporary Egyptian art, as seen in the work of Rasha Amin, whose Cairo upbringing shapes her multidisciplinary pieces, reflecting the influence of Egypt’s rich cultural heritage.[139]",1102,,,,,,,cursor_leave,,
