39,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,45,Female,sg_1776252886614_ey90wo,clumpy,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,article_open,2026-04-15T11:59:08.707Z,Contemporary_art,Contemporary art,,4804,search,,,,,,,,,,,,
39,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,45,Female,sg_1776252886614_ey90wo,clumpy,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,paste,2026-04-15T11:59:25.329Z,,,,,,,,,,,"Contemporary art is generally art created from the 1970s onwards. Contemporary artists work in a globally influenced, culturally diverse, and technologically advancing world. Their art is a dynamic combination of materials, methods, concepts, and subjects that continue the challenging of boundaries that was already well underway in the 20th century. Diverse and eclectic, contemporary art as a whole is distinguished by the very lack of a uniform, organising principle, ideology, or ""-ism"". Contemporary art is part of a cultural dialogue that concerns larger contextual frameworks such as personal and cultural identity, family, community, and nationality.

In English, modern and contemporary are synonyms, resulting in some conflation and confusion of the terms modern art and contemporary art by non-specialists.[1] The latter is the art of today. Some specialists also consider that the frontier between the two is blurry; for instance, the French Musée National d'Art Moderne does not differentiate them in its collections.[2]",1036,,,,,
