41,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,25,Female,sg_1776253063412_swmccm,clumpy,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,article_open,2026-04-15T12:05:52.120Z,Renaissance_art,Renaissance art,,6483,link_click,,,,,,,,,,,,
41,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,25,Female,sg_1776253063412_swmccm,clumpy,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T12:07:42.946Z,,,,,,,"The main role that ancient art plays in the modern day is supporting our understanding of how life was in the past. Archeology has enabled us to find pottery, remains, art, symbolic artefacts that have allowed us deeper insight into the culture of different eras. For example, we understand from ancient Egyptian art found that they had a much more sophisticated understanding of anatomy and paid close attention to detail, so we may infer that they were more highly educated and had the ability to undertake research. 
There are elements of ancient art that are still adopted today such as styles (neolithic), and certain painting traditions that are still employed today, such as the Tomb of the Diver. We often display these works of art in museums to ensure that people do not forget them, and can appreciate the beauty of seeing them.",839,,,,,,,debounce,,
