43,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,58,Male,sg_1776254020940_70tgcw,diffuse,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T12:22:18.622Z,,,,,,,"In essence, surviving, ancient works of art contain an extraordinary variety of incredible influences. Many of these ancient masterpieces are often unparalled in the inspiration and sense of historical perspective they give to modern society. 

The older the art, arguably the more the inspiration for example in caves in Iran's Lorestan province exhibit painted imagery of animals and hunting scenes include paintings that are 5,000 years old and are interpreted and copied by modern artist continuously.

The ancient Greeks also produced a plethora of superb artwork (potter, metalwork, architecture etc) that is entirely inspirational to this day but also stimulates the idea of culture and order back into the depths of time.",729,,,,,,,debounce,,
