44,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,30,Male,sg_1776254146768_qlli4f,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T12:06:41.435Z,,,,,,,"Ancient art comes in a wide range of styles and can be seen all throughout contemporary society. A prominent type is Romanesque art, prominent in the 11th and 12th centuries, it helped shape modern Europe into what it is today",226,,,,,,,debounce,,
44,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,30,Male,sg_1776254146768_qlli4f,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot_cursor_leave,2026-04-15T12:07:00.915Z,,,,,,,"Ancient art comes in a wide range of styles and can be seen all throughout contemporary society. A prominent type is Romanesque art, prominent in the 11th and 12th centuries, it helped shape modern Europe into what it is today",226,,,,,,,cursor_leave,,
44,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,30,Male,sg_1776254146768_qlli4f,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,paste,2026-04-15T12:07:15.961Z,,,,,,,,,,,"Combining features of ancient Roman and Byzantine buildings and other local traditions, Romanesque architecture is known by its massive quality, thick walls, round arches, sturdy pillars, barrel vaults, large towers and decorative arcading",239,,,,,
44,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,30,Male,sg_1776254146768_qlli4f,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T12:07:17.964Z,,,,,,,"Ancient art comes in a wide range of styles and can be seen all throughout contemporary society. A prominent type is Romanesque art, prominent in the 11th and 12th centuries, it helped shape modern Europe into what it is today. Combining features of ancient Roman and Byzantine buildings and other local traditions, Romanesque architecture is known by its massive quality, thick walls, round arches, sturdy pillars, barrel vaults, large towers and decorative arcading",467,,,,,,,debounce,,
44,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,30,Male,sg_1776254146768_qlli4f,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot_cursor_leave,2026-04-15T12:07:39.766Z,,,,,,,"Ancient art comes in a wide range of styles and can be seen all throughout contemporary society. A prominent type is Romanesque art, prominent in the 11th and 12th centuries, it helped shape modern Europe into what it is today. Combining features of ancient Roman and Byzantine buildings and other local traditions, Romanesque architecture is known by its massive quality, thick walls, round arches, sturdy pillars, barrel vaults, large towers and decorative arcading",467,,,,,,,cursor_leave,,
44,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,30,Male,sg_1776254146768_qlli4f,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,paste,2026-04-15T12:07:48.967Z,,,,,,,,,,,"in 1813 William Gunn used the term to broadly describe the pre-Gothic architecture of the Western Europe, all the way from the 4th century to the 12th.[4] Gunn's work, An Inquiry into the Origin and Influence of Gothic Architecture (London 1819), was published later,[9] in 1819.[10][11] The word was used by Gunn to describe the style that was identifiably medieval and prefigured the Gothic, yet maintained the rounded Roman arch and thus appeared to be a continuation of the Roman tradition of building;",506,,,,,
44,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,30,Male,sg_1776254146768_qlli4f,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T12:07:50.970Z,,,,,,,"Ancient art comes in a wide range of styles and can be seen all throughout contemporary society. A prominent type is Romanesque art, prominent in the 11th and 12th centuries, it helped shape modern Europe into what it is today. Combining features of ancient Roman and Byzantine buildings and other local traditions, Romanesque architecture is known by its massive quality, thick walls, round arches, sturdy pillars, barrel vaults, large towers and decorative arcading. in 1813 William Gunn used the term to broadly describe the pre-Gothic architecture of the Western Europe, all the way from the 4th century to the 12th.[4] Gunn's work, An Inquiry into the Origin and Influence of Gothic Architecture (London 1819), was published later,[9] in 1819.[10][11] The word was used by Gunn to describe the style that was identifiably medieval and prefigured the Gothic, yet maintained the rounded Roman arch and thus appeared to be a continuation of the Roman tradition of building;",975,,,,,,,debounce,,
44,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,30,Male,sg_1776254146768_qlli4f,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T12:07:55.943Z,,,,,,,"Ancient art comes in a wide range of styles and can be seen all throughout contemporary society. A prominent type is Romanesque art, prominent in the 11th and 12th centuries, it helped shape modern Europe into what it is today. Combining features of ancient Roman and Byzantine buildings and other local traditions, Romanesque architecture is known by its massive quality, thick walls, round arches, sturdy pillars, barrel vaults, large towers and decorative arcading. in 1813 William Gunn used the term to broadly describe the pre-Gothic architecture of the Western Europe, all the way from the 4th century to the 12th.[4] Gunn's work, An Inquiry into the Origin and Influence of Gothic Architecture (London 1819), was published later,[9] in 1819.[10][11] The word was used by Gunn to describe the style that was identifiably medieval and prefigured the Gothic, yet maintained the rounded Roman arch and thus appeared to be a continuation of the Roman tradition of building.",975,,,,,,,debounce,,
44,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,30,Male,sg_1776254146768_qlli4f,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot_cursor_leave,2026-04-15T12:07:56.217Z,,,,,,,"Ancient art comes in a wide range of styles and can be seen all throughout contemporary society. A prominent type is Romanesque art, prominent in the 11th and 12th centuries, it helped shape modern Europe into what it is today. Combining features of ancient Roman and Byzantine buildings and other local traditions, Romanesque architecture is known by its massive quality, thick walls, round arches, sturdy pillars, barrel vaults, large towers and decorative arcading. in 1813 William Gunn used the term to broadly describe the pre-Gothic architecture of the Western Europe, all the way from the 4th century to the 12th.[4] Gunn's work, An Inquiry into the Origin and Influence of Gothic Architecture (London 1819), was published later,[9] in 1819.[10][11] The word was used by Gunn to describe the style that was identifiably medieval and prefigured the Gothic, yet maintained the rounded Roman arch and thus appeared to be a continuation of the Roman tradition of building.",975,,,,,,,cursor_leave,,
44,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,30,Male,sg_1776254146768_qlli4f,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot_cursor_leave,2026-04-15T12:09:28.667Z,,,,,,,"Ancient art comes in a wide range of styles and can be seen all throughout contemporary society. A prominent type is Romanesque art, prominent in the 11th and 12th centuries, it helped shape modern Europe into what it is today. Combining features of ancient Roman and Byzantine buildings and other local traditions, Romanesque architecture is known by its massive quality, thick walls, round arches, sturdy pillars, barrel vaults, large towers and decorative arcading. in 1813 William Gunn used the term to broadly describe the pre-Gothic architecture of the Western Europe, all the way from the 4th century to the 12th.[4] Gunn's work, An Inquiry into the Origin and Influence of Gothic Architecture (London 1819), was published later,[9] in 1819.[10][11] The word was used by Gunn to describe the style that was identifiably medieval and prefigured the Gothic, yet maintained the rounded Roman arch and thus appeared to be a continuation of the Roman tradition of building.",975,,,,,,,cursor_leave,,
44,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,30,Male,sg_1776254146768_qlli4f,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,paste,2026-04-15T12:09:33.165Z,,,,,,,,,,,"Buildings of every type were constructed in the Romanesque style, with evidence remaining of simple domestic buildings, elegant town houses, grand palaces, commercial premises, civic buildings, castles, city walls, bridges, village churches, abbey churches, abbey complexes and large cathedrals.[24] Of these types of buildings, domestic and commercial buildings are the most rare, with only a handful of survivors in the United Kingdom, several clusters in France, isolated buildings across Europe and by far the largest number, often unidentified and altered over the centuries, in Italy. Many castles exist, the foundations of which date from the Romanesque period. Most have been substantially altered, and many are in ruins",728,,,,,
44,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,30,Male,sg_1776254146768_qlli4f,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T12:09:35.167Z,,,,,,,"Ancient art comes in a wide range of styles and can be seen all throughout contemporary society. A prominent type is Romanesque art, prominent in the 11th and 12th centuries, it helped shape modern Europe into what it is today. Combining features of ancient Roman and Byzantine buildings and other local traditions, Romanesque architecture is known by its massive quality, thick walls, round arches, sturdy pillars, barrel vaults, large towers and decorative arcading. in 1813 William Gunn used the term to broadly describe the pre-Gothic architecture of the Western Europe, all the way from the 4th century to the 12th.[4] Gunn's work, An Inquiry into the Origin and Influence of Gothic Architecture (London 1819), was published later,[9] in 1819.[10][11] The word was used by Gunn to describe the style that was identifiably medieval and prefigured the Gothic, yet maintained the rounded Roman arch and thus appeared to be a continuation of the Roman tradition of building. Buildings of every type were constructed in the Romanesque style, with evidence remaining of simple domestic buildings, elegant town houses, grand palaces, commercial premises, civic buildings, castles, city walls, bridges, village churches, abbey churches, abbey complexes and large cathedrals.[24] Of these types of buildings, domestic and commercial buildings are the most rare, with only a handful of survivors in the United Kingdom, several clusters in France, isolated buildings across Europe and by far the largest number, often unidentified and altered over the centuries, in Italy. Many castles exist, the foundations of which date from the Romanesque period. Most have been substantially altered, and many are in ruins",1704,,,,,,,debounce,,
