46,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,25,Female,sg_1776254581039_yuaf3i,diffuse,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,article_open,2026-04-15T12:28:43.798Z,Metropolitan_Museum_of_Art,Metropolitan Museum of Art,,25318,search,,,,,,,,,,,,
46,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,25,Female,sg_1776254581039_yuaf3i,diffuse,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,paste,2026-04-15T12:32:08.541Z,,,,,,,,,,,"With some 13,000 artworks, primarily by European and American artists, the modern art collection occupies 60,000 square feet (6,000 m2), of gallery space[115] and contains many iconic modern works. Cornerstones of the collection include Picasso's portrait of Gertrude Stein, Jasper Johns's White Flag, Jackson Pollock's Autumn Rhythm (Number 30), and Max Beckmann's triptych Beginning. Certain artists are represented in remarkable depth, for a museum whose focus is not exclusively on modern art: for example, ninety works constitute the museum's Paul Klee collection, donated by Heinz Berggruen, spanning the entirety of the artist's life.[116] Due to the Met's long history, ""contemporary"" paintings acquired in years past have often migrated to other collections at the museum, particularly to the American and European Paintings departments.[117]

In April 2013, it was reported that the museum was to receive a collection worth $1 billion (~$1.32 billion in 2024) from cosmetics tycoon Leonard Lauder. The collection of Cubist art includes work by Pablo Picasso, Georges Braque and Juan Gris and went on display in 2014.[118] The Met has since added to the collection, for example spending $31.8 million (~$39 million in 2024) for Gris' The musician's table in 2018.[119]",1279,,,,,
