In April 2013, it was reported that the museum was to receive a collection worth $1 billion (~$1.32 billion in 2024) from cosmetics tycoon Leonard Lauder. The collection of Cubist art includes work by Pablo Picasso, Georges Braque and Juan Gris and went on display in 2014.[118] The Met has since added to the collection, for example spending $31.8 million (~$39 million in 2024) for Gris' The musician's table in 2018.[119]",1277,,,,,,,debounce,,
