53,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,49,Female,sg_1776256452227_mshq8o,diffuse,0,1,practice,practice-capybaras,What do Capybaras eat?,paste,2026-04-15T12:39:46.661Z,,,,,,,,,,,"They eat a greater variety of plants during the dry season, as fewer plants are available. While they eat grass during the wet season, they have to switch to more abundant reeds during the dry season.[26] Plants that capybaras eat during the summer lose their nutritional value in the winter, so they are not consumed at that time",330,,,,,
53,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,49,Female,sg_1776256452227_mshq8o,diffuse,0,1,practice,practice-capybaras,What do Capybaras eat?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T12:39:48.668Z,,,,,,,"Capybaras are herbivores. Herbivores are animals which have evolved to feed on plants. Capybaras eat mainly grasses and aquatic plants such as water lilies, as well as fruit and tree bark. They eat a greater variety of plants during the dry season, as fewer plants are available. While they eat grass during the wet season, they have to switch to more abundant reeds during the dry season.[26] Plants that capybaras eat during the summer lose their nutritional value in the winter, so they are not consumed at that time",519,,,,,,,debounce,,
53,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,49,Female,sg_1776256452227_mshq8o,diffuse,0,1,practice,practice-capybaras,What do Capybaras eat?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T12:39:53.266Z,,,,,,,"Capybaras are herbivores. Herbivores are animals which have evolved to feed on plants. Capybaras eat mainly grasses and aquatic plants such as water lilies, as well as fruit and tree bark. They eat a greater variety of plants during the dry season, as fewer plants are available. While they eat grass during the wet season, they have to switch to more abundant reeds during the dry season. Plants that capybaras eat during the summer lose their nutritional value in the winter, so they are not consumed at that time.",516,,,,,,,debounce,,
53,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,49,Female,sg_1776256452227_mshq8o,diffuse,0,1,practice,practice-capybaras,What do Capybaras eat?,answer_snapshot_cursor_leave,2026-04-15T12:39:57.013Z,,,,,,,"Capybaras are herbivores. Herbivores are animals which have evolved to feed on plants. Capybaras eat mainly grasses and aquatic plants such as water lilies, as well as fruit and tree bark. They eat a greater variety of plants during the dry season, as fewer plants are available. While they eat grass during the wet season, they have to switch to more abundant reeds during the dry season. Plants that capybaras eat during the summer lose their nutritional value in the winter, so they are not consumed at that time.",516,,,,,,,cursor_leave,,
53,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,49,Female,sg_1776256452227_mshq8o,diffuse,0,1,practice,practice-capybaras,What do Capybaras eat?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T12:40:17.225Z,,,,,,,"Capybaras are herbivores. Herbivores are animals which have evolved to feed on plants. Capybaras eat mainly grasses and aquatic plants such as water lilies, as well as fruit and tree bark. They eat a greater variety of plants during the dry season, as fewer plants are available. While they eat grass during the wet season, they have to switch to more abundant reeds during the dry season. Plants that capybaras eat during the summer lose their nutritional value in the winter, so they are not consumed at that time. ",517,,,,,,,debounce,,
53,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,49,Female,sg_1776256452227_mshq8o,diffuse,0,1,practice,practice-capybaras,What do Capybaras eat?,paste,2026-04-15T12:40:17.761Z,,,,,,,,,,,"Capybaras are autocoprophagous,[28] meaning they eat their own feces as a source of bacterial gut flora, to help digest the cellulose in the grass that forms their normal diet, and to extract the maximum protein and vitamins from their food. They also regurgitate food to masticate again, similar to cud-chewing by cattle.",322,,,,,
53,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,49,Female,sg_1776256452227_mshq8o,diffuse,0,1,practice,practice-capybaras,What do Capybaras eat?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T12:40:19.774Z,,,,,,,"Capybaras are herbivores. Herbivores are animals which have evolved to feed on plants. Capybaras eat mainly grasses and aquatic plants such as water lilies, as well as fruit and tree bark. They eat a greater variety of plants during the dry season, as fewer plants are available. While they eat grass during the wet season, they have to switch to more abundant reeds during the dry season. Plants that capybaras eat during the summer lose their nutritional value in the winter, so they are not consumed at that time. Capybaras are autocoprophagous,[28] meaning they eat their own feces as a source of bacterial gut flora, to help digest the cellulose in the grass that forms their normal diet, and to extract the maximum protein and vitamins from their food. They also regurgitate food to masticate again, similar to cud-chewing by cattle.",839,,,,,,,debounce,,
