54,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,42,Female,sg_1776256953248_y9fw8r,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T13:02:18.316Z,,,,,,,"Art marks the transition of one time period to another. For example, Renaissance art marks the transition of Europe from the medieval period to the Early Modern age. They also help influence artistic techniques. Some examples are the use of foreshortening to create depth was invented during the renaissance period. It also can show us what ideals and beliefs society held throughout history, based on what is depicted in the art as well as the style of the art. For example,",475,,,,,,,debounce,,
54,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,42,Female,sg_1776256953248_y9fw8r,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot_cursor_leave,2026-04-15T13:02:36.153Z,,,,,,,"Art marks the transition of one time period to another. For example, Renaissance art marks the transition of Europe from the medieval period to the Early Modern age. They also help influence artistic techniques. Some examples are the use of foreshortening to create depth was invented during the renaissance period. It also can show us what ideals and beliefs society held throughout history, based on what is depicted in the art as well as the style of the art. For example,",475,,,,,,,cursor_leave,,
54,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,42,Female,sg_1776256953248_y9fw8r,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,paste,2026-04-15T13:02:54.355Z,,,,,,,,,,,"Painting of the High Renaissance is considered to be the absolute zenith of western painting[22] and achieved the balancing and reconciliation, in harmony, of contradictory and seemingly mutually exclusive artistic positions, such as real versus ideal, movement versus rest, freedom versus law, space versus plane, and line versus colour.[",339,,,,,
54,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,42,Female,sg_1776256953248_y9fw8r,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T13:02:56.360Z,,,,,,,"Art marks the transition of one time period to another. For example, Renaissance art marks the transition of Europe from the medieval period to the Early Modern age. They also help influence artistic techniques. Some examples are the use of foreshortening to create depth was invented during the renaissance period. It also can show us what ideals and beliefs society held throughout history, based on what is depicted in the art as well as the style of the art. For example,Painting of the High Renaissance is considered to be the absolute zenith of western painting[22] and achieved the balancing and reconciliation, in harmony, of contradictory and seemingly mutually exclusive artistic positions, such as real versus ideal, movement versus rest, freedom versus law, space versus plane, and line versus colour.[",814,,,,,,,debounce,,
54,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,42,Female,sg_1776256953248_y9fw8r,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T13:03:00.173Z,,,,,,,"Art marks the transition of one time period to another. For example, Renaissance art marks the transition of Europe from the medieval period to the Early Modern age. They also help influence artistic techniques. Some examples are the use of foreshortening to create depth was invented during the renaissance period. It also can show us what ideals and beliefs society held throughout history, based on what is depicted in the art as well as the style of the art. For example, painting of the High Renaissance is considered to be the absolute zenith of western painting[22] and achieved the balancing and reconciliation, in harmony, of contradictory and seemingly mutually exclusive artistic positions, such as real versus ideal, movement versus rest, freedom versus law, space versus plane, and line versus colour.[",815,,,,,,,debounce,,
54,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,42,Female,sg_1776256953248_y9fw8r,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T13:03:05.530Z,,,,,,,"Art marks the transition of one time period to another. For example, Renaissance art marks the transition of Europe from the medieval period to the Early Modern age. They also help influence artistic techniques. Some examples are the use of foreshortening to create depth was invented during the renaissance period. It also can show us what ideals and beliefs society held throughout history, based on what is depicted in the art as well as the style of the art. For example, painting of the High Renaissance is considered to be the absolute zenith of western painting[22] and achieved the balancing and reconciliation, in harmony, of contradictory and seemingly mutually exclusive artistic positions, such as real versus ideal, movement versus rest, freedom versus law, space versus plane, and line versus colour.",814,,,,,,,debounce,,
54,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,42,Female,sg_1776256953248_y9fw8r,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T13:03:29.602Z,,,,,,,"Art marks the transition of one time period to another. For example, Renaissance art marks the transition of Europe from the medieval period to the Early Modern age. They also help influence artistic techniques. Some examples are the use of foreshortening to create depth was invented during the renaissance period. It also can show us what ideals and beliefs society held throughout history, based on what is depicted in the art as well as the style of the art. For example, painting of the High Renaissance is considered to be the absolute zenith of western painting[22] and achieved the balancing and reconciliation, in harmony, of contradictory and seemingly mutually exclusive artistic positions, such as real versus ideal, movement versus rest, freedom versus law, space versus plane, and line versus colour.",814,,,,,,,submit,,
54,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,42,Female,sg_1776256953248_y9fw8r,diffuse,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,task_end,2026-04-15T13:03:29.602Z,,,,,,,,,"Art marks the transition of one time period to another. For example, Renaissance art marks the transition of Europe from the medieval period to the Early Modern age. They also help influence artistic techniques. Some examples are the use of foreshortening to create depth was invented during the renaissance period. It also can show us what ideals and beliefs society held throughout history, based on what is depicted in the art as well as the style of the art. For example, painting of the High Renaissance is considered to be the absolute zenith of western painting[22] and achieved the balancing and reconciliation, in harmony, of contradictory and seemingly mutually exclusive artistic positions, such as real versus ideal, movement versus rest, freedom versus law, space versus plane, and line versus colour.",814,,,,,,,
