54,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,42,Female,sg_1776256953248_y9fw8r,diffuse,2,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T13:11:31.750Z,,,,,,,"Unexpected scientific findings were found to activate the prefrontal cortex as well as the left hemisphere in general. This suggests that unexpected discoveries provoke more attention. Also, Linear reasoning functions of language such as grammar and word production are often lateralized to the left hemisphere of the brain, which makes sense since science involves reasoning. ",377,,,,,,,debounce,,
54,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,42,Female,sg_1776256953248_y9fw8r,diffuse,2,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T13:12:10.827Z,,,,,,,"Unexpected scientific findings were found to activate the prefrontal cortex as well as the left hemisphere in general. This suggests that unexpected discoveries provoke more attention. Also, Linear reasoning functions of language such as grammar and word production are often lateralized to the left hemisphere of the brain, which makes sense since science involves reasoning. The prefrontal cortex is responsible for higher-order cognitive functions such as memory, risk processing, and speech formation",504,,,,,,,debounce,,
