55,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,44,Male,sg_1776257206753_yo7kb8,clumpy,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,familiarity_rating,2026-04-15T13:01:39.648Z,,,,,,,,,,,,,1,1,,,
55,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,44,Male,sg_1776257206753_yo7kb8,clumpy,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,task_start,2026-04-15T13:01:41.559Z,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
55,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,44,Male,sg_1776257206753_yo7kb8,clumpy,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,search,2026-04-15T13:01:52.173Z,,,,,,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,,,,,,,,,,,
55,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,44,Male,sg_1776257206753_yo7kb8,clumpy,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,article_open,2026-04-15T13:05:06.926Z,Metropolitan_Museum_of_Art,Metropolitan Museum of Art,,25318,search,,,,,,,,,,,,
55,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,44,Male,sg_1776257206753_yo7kb8,clumpy,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot_cursor_leave,2026-04-15T13:07:56.600Z,,,,,,,"The Metropolitan Museum of Art, colloquially referred to as the Met, is an encyclopedic art museum in New York City. By floor area, it is the fourth-largest museum in the world and the largest art museum in the Americas. With 5,727,258 visitors in fiscal year 2025, it was the most-visited museum in the United States and the fourth-most visited art museum in the world.[7]

In 2000, its permanent collection had over two million works;[1] it currently lists a total of 1.5 million works.[8] The collection is divided into 17 curatorial departments. The main building at 1000 Fifth Avenue, along the Museum Mile on the eastern edge of Central Park on Manhattan's Upper East Side, is by area one of the world's largest art museums. The first portion of the approximately 2-million-square-foot (190,000 m2) building was built in 1880. A much smaller second location, The Cloisters at Fort Tryon Park in Upper Manhattan, contains an extensive collection of art, architecture, and artifacts from medieval Europe.

The Metropolitan Museum of Art was founded in 1870. The museum was established by a group of Americans, including philanthropists, artists, and businessmen, with the goal of creating a national institution that would inspire and educate the public.[9] The museum's permanent collection consists of works of art ranging from the ancient Near East and ancient Egypt, through classical antiquity to the contemporary world. It includes paintings, sculptures, and graphic works from many European Old Masters, as well as an extensive collection of American, modern, and contemporary art. The Met also maintains extensive holdings of African, Asian, Oceanian, Byzantine, and Islamic art. The museum is home to encyclopedic collections of musical instruments, costumes, and decorative arts and textiles, as well as antique weapons and armor from around the world. Several notable interiors, ranging from 1st-century Rome through modern American design, are installed in its galleries.",1987,,,,,,,cursor_leave,,
55,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,44,Male,sg_1776257206753_yo7kb8,clumpy,2,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T13:11:44.275Z,,,,,,,"The Metropolitan Museum of Art, colloquially referred to as the Met, is an encyclopedic art museum in New York City. By floor area, it is the fourth-largest museum in the world and the largest art museum in the Americas. With 5,727,258 visitors in fiscal year 2025, it was the most-visited museum in the United States and the fourth-most visited art museum in the world.[7]

