56,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,41,Female,sg_1776257219882_ivri1v,clumpy,1,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,article_open,2026-04-15T12:55:38.799Z,Neuroplasticity,Neuroplasticity,,16389,search,,,,,,,,,,,,
56,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,41,Female,sg_1776257219882_ivri1v,clumpy,1,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,paste,2026-04-15T12:55:57.975Z,,,,,,,,,,,"Neuroplasticity refers to the brain's ability to reorganize and rewire its neural connections, enabling it to adapt and function in ways that differ from its prior state. This process can occur in response to learning new skills, experiencing environmental changes, recovering from injuries, or adapting to sensory or cognitive deficits. Such adaptability highlights the dynamic and ever-evolving nature of the brain, even into adulthood",437,,,,,
56,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,41,Female,sg_1776257219882_ivri1v,clumpy,1,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T12:55:59.986Z,,,,,,,"Neuroplasticity refers to the brain's ability to reorganize and rewire its neural connections, enabling it to adapt and function in ways that differ from its prior state. This process can occur in response to learning new skills, experiencing environmental changes, recovering from injuries, or adapting to sensory or cognitive deficits. Such adaptability highlights the dynamic and ever-evolving nature of the brain, even into adulthood",437,,,,,,,debounce,,
56,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,41,Female,sg_1776257219882_ivri1v,clumpy,1,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,answer_snapshot_cursor_leave,2026-04-15T12:56:09.073Z,,,,,,,"Neuroplasticity refers to the brain's ability to reorganize and rewire its neural connections, enabling it to adapt and function in ways that differ from its prior state. This process can occur in response to learning new skills, experiencing environmental changes, recovering from injuries, or adapting to sensory or cognitive deficits. Such adaptability highlights the dynamic and ever-evolving nature of the brain, even into adulthood",437,,,,,,,cursor_leave,,
56,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,41,Female,sg_1776257219882_ivri1v,clumpy,1,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,paste,2026-04-15T12:56:19.106Z,,,,,,,,,,,"Neuroplasticity was once thought by neuroscientists to manifest only during childhood,[9][10] but research in the later half of the 20th century showed that many aspects of the brain exhibit plasticity through adulthood.",220,,,,,
56,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,41,Female,sg_1776257219882_ivri1v,clumpy,1,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T12:56:21.114Z,,,,,,,"Neuroplasticity refers to the brain's ability to reorganize and rewire its neural connections, enabling it to adapt and function in ways that differ from its prior state. This process can occur in response to learning new skills, experiencing environmental changes, recovering from injuries, or adapting to sensory or cognitive deficits. Such adaptability highlights the dynamic and ever-evolving nature of the brain, even into adulthood.

As an example of new discoveries - Neuroplasticity was once thought by neuroscientists to manifest only during childhood,[9][10] but research in the later half of the 20th century showed that many aspects of the brain exhibit plasticity through adulthood.",695,,,,,,,debounce,,
