59,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,21,Male,sg_1776257622048_utieoi,clumpy,0,1,practice,practice-capybaras,What do Capybaras eat?,paste,2026-04-15T13:01:09.747Z,,,,,,,,,,,"They eat a greater variety of plants during the dry season, as fewer plants are available. While they eat grass during the wet season, they have to switch to more abundant reeds during the dry season.",200,,,,,
59,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,21,Male,sg_1776257622048_utieoi,clumpy,0,1,practice,practice-capybaras,What do Capybaras eat?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T13:01:13.596Z,,,,,,,"Capybaras are known as herbivores; this means their diet primarily consists of grass, aquatic plants, fruit and tree bark. The capybara has a tendency to be quite selective - they'll feed on the leaves of one species and disregard other species surrounding it. This diet changes depending on the season. To explain, they eat a greater variety of plants during the dry season, as fewer plants are available. While they eat grass during the wet season, they have to switch to more abundant reeds during the dry season.",516,,,,,,,debounce,,
