59,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,21,Male,sg_1776257622048_utieoi,clumpy,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,article_open,2026-04-15T13:11:26.384Z,Church_of_the_Nativity,Church of the Nativity,,9293,link_click,,,,,,,,,,,,
59,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,21,Male,sg_1776257622048_utieoi,clumpy,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,paste,2026-04-15T13:11:27.144Z,,,,,,,,,,,"With the building of Christian basilicas in the late 4th century, wall and ceiling mosaics were adopted for Christian uses. The earliest examples of Christian basilicas have not survived, but the mosaics of Santa Constanza and Santa Pudenziana, both from the 4th century, still exist.",284,,,,,
59,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,21,Male,sg_1776257622048_utieoi,clumpy,1,,art_history,high-art-history,How do ancient works of art play a role in contemporary society?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T13:11:29.158Z,,,,,,,"Ancient works of art play a very large role within contemporary society, as we can observe not just its evolution into what we see today, but also observe examples that make parallels in that of modern art, and how that affects our society. For example, look at mosaics; a mosaic is a pattern or image made of small regular or irregular pieces of colored stone, glass or ceramic, held in place by plaster/mortar, and covering a surface. Mosaics are often used as floor and wall decoration, and were particularly popular in the Ancient Roman world. One might assume that this art form is outdated, but it now holds a parallel to video game pixel art and pop culture. Not only is this art form still relevant in its style, but also in its depictions. Much of what it shows includes depictions of Christian works, which, for many people, still holds importance as being one of the most popular religions to date, and has a large influence over people's decisions. With the building of Christian basilicas in the late 4th century, wall and ceiling mosaics were adopted for Christian uses. The earliest examples of Christian basilicas have not survived, but the mosaics of Santa Constanza and Santa Pudenziana, both from the 4th century, still exist.",1245,,,,,,,debounce,,
