61,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,47,Male,sg_1776257759053_1czqc2,diffuse,1,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,article_open,2026-04-15T13:05:59.822Z,Human_brain,Human brain,,25482,search,,,,,,,,,,,,
61,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,47,Male,sg_1776257759053_1czqc2,diffuse,1,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,paste,2026-04-15T13:07:35.906Z,,,,,,,,,,,"The cells of the brain include neurons and supportive glial cells. There are more than 86 billion neurons in the brain, and a more or less equal number of other cells. Brain activity is made possible by the interconnections of neurons and their release of neurotransmitters in response to nerve impulses. Neurons connect to form neural pathways, neural circuits, and elaborate network systems. The whole circuitry is driven by the process of neurotransmission.",460,,,,,
61,Wikipedia_Exp_14.04,Wikipedia_Exp_13.04,47,Male,sg_1776257759053_1czqc2,diffuse,1,,psychology,high-psychology,What brain mechanisms help people make scientific discoveries?,answer_snapshot,2026-04-15T13:07:37.917Z,,,,,,,"The cells of the brain include neurons and supportive glial cells. There are more than 86 billion neurons in the brain, and a more or less equal number of other cells. Brain activity is made possible by the interconnections of neurons and their release of neurotransmitters in response to nerve impulses. Neurons connect to form neural pathways, neural circuits, and elaborate network systems. The whole circuitry is driven by the process of neurotransmission.",460,,,,,,,debounce,,
